{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"1c38848263c14622","type":"text","text":"Create the logic","x":-420,"y":160,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c47b78fc3b1e568b","type":"text","text":"CardName\nDisplayed name for the card.","x":-1680,"y":-384,"width":310,"height":91},
		{"id":"dd65215860c95493","type":"text","text":"<span style=\"font-size:40px\">EXPORT\nVARIABLES","x":-1020,"y":110,"width":260,"height":150,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"7f6e3a9d933b4a72","type":"text","text":"CardType\nHow the card behaves in battle. Mouseover the variable to see explanation for what types there are.","x":-1620,"y":-280,"width":250,"height":160},
		{"id":"38ae5b78c80f2b71","type":"text","text":"SubTypeStr\nUsed in ConditionalComponent: ifSubtype","x":-1680,"y":-85,"width":310,"height":105},
		{"id":"1ac2d5d3b83e548f","type":"text","text":"Group\nDetermines which loot and shop table can the card be found in. Cards that cannot be permanently acquired should have their Group set to NONE","x":-1672,"y":63,"width":302,"height":197},
		{"id":"2f530fd671d02648","type":"text","text":"AI Behavior\nDetermines how the AI uses the card. Mouseover variables to see what they do.","x":-1680,"y":555,"width":250,"height":176},
		{"id":"b444b4b421524084","type":"text","text":"Upgrade Paths\nHow a card can be upgraded.","x":-1680,"y":780,"width":250,"height":96},
		{"id":"da1e7a4af2271c1c","type":"text","text":"Card Upgrading","x":-2240,"y":415,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"b088f0c1b2dd4779","type":"text","text":"If a Alt Card Name field is left blank, that upgrade path is considered not to exist.","x":-2240,"y":525,"width":250,"height":118},
		{"id":"ec906447659ea8ec","type":"text","text":"If you want to change the Actions of an upgraded card, just Duplicate the Actions node and assign the new node to an Alt Actions Node variable. Then setup the logic under it as you see fit.","x":-2270,"y":695,"width":310,"height":181},
		{"id":"7ef81902c4d8d07d","type":"text","text":"ManaCost","x":-1650,"y":280,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4338ae1e3c552c22","type":"text","text":"StartingHealth","x":-1650,"y":355,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"2d1a757f2e83f0a7","type":"text","text":"StartingDamage","x":-1650,"y":445,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c8ca0b38754e49e6","type":"text","text":"Card Logic","x":-111,"y":165,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"e96234e1414147ff","type":"text","text":"Does the Actions node have at least 1 Trigger child?","x":202,"y":160,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"cab999b73d062c41","type":"text","text":"Does the Trigger receive the signal in its triggered_when variable?","x":570,"y":140,"width":290,"height":100},
		{"id":"174488965a0f5c7a","type":"text","text":"Do all of the Trigger's ConditionalComponent children return True based on the signal's SignalParams?","x":985,"y":121,"width":275,"height":139},
		{"id":"b486600319b51d58","type":"text","text":"Your triggers determine z in a card's effect text that goes 'on z, do x to group y. They operate independently from the Card itself, with a few exceptions.","x":590,"y":300,"width":250,"height":186},
		{"id":"400ccdd0aa066b16","type":"text","text":"Nothing happens.","x":998,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7f74d365c086ff47","type":"text","text":"The card does nothing","x":202,"y":-5,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"c77beb64510be521","type":"text","text":"These ConditionalComponents should be saved as part of the Trigger scene. They are mostly things that are obvious to the player, but not to the computer. For example, an IfSelf CondComponent under a Trigger checks if the signal was emitted by the same card as the one with the Trigger.","x":943,"y":363,"width":360,"height":215},
		{"id":"b5211e747a7bafa2","type":"text","text":"So you want to..","x":-2179,"y":1242,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4ff914e5812eb629","type":"text","text":"Create an On-Turn effect","x":-2179,"y":1382,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"672866f7d4fa64d5","type":"text","text":"Start by adding an On Allied Turn Trigger as a child to the Actions node. It has 'turnStarted' as its triggered_when value. It comes with a ConditionalComponent child which checks is the turn that just started is the turn of the given card's owner.","x":-2286,"y":1512,"width":465,"height":160},
		{"id":"1725886b438e38a1","type":"text","text":"Trigger presets can be found in the Triggers folder.","x":-1585,"y":1562,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"99e19e86fdec65d7","type":"text","text":"Add a CardAction as a child to your OnAlliedTurnTrigger with the Add Child Node (+) button. You can have multiple of them. You need one CardAction for each effect with a different set of targets from the others.","x":-2252,"y":1742,"width":398,"height":160},
		{"id":"eb20359d68f4e73e","type":"text","text":"You want an AutoTargetingComponent when you want your effect to be applied to cards automatically, without prompting the player's input. Cards affected are  Add ConditionalComponents to it as children to set them up.  Some simplest AutoTargetingComponent presets can be found in the Targeting Components folder.","x":-1665,"y":1923,"width":409,"height":231},
		{"id":"0e954efc3806a97c","type":"text","text":"Conditional Components can be found in the Conditionals folder.","x":-1086,"y":1989,"width":250,"height":99},
		{"id":"253551e433b8d35e","type":"text","text":"Add any number of Skill children to your CardAction. All of them would be applied to each card in the list returned by your TargetingComponent.","x":-2243,"y":2202,"width":380,"height":140},
		{"id":"713d092651d0aecf","type":"text","text":"Skill presets can be found in the Actions folder.","x":-1585,"y":2242,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8f6e384ed30bc53d","type":"text","text":"Add an AutoTargetingComponent type scene and drag it under your CardAction. ","x":-2243,"y":2004,"width":380,"height":70},
		{"id":"1baf1e4edd3a1903","type":"text","text":"So you want to...","x":-2178,"y":2482,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3a3d98e95aa84331","type":"text","text":"Rituals can be designed in exactly the same way. Just set the card's type to RITUAL in the main node's settings.","x":-1683,"y":2572,"width":250,"height":160},
		{"id":"40e6f4daf87cd401","type":"text","text":"Create a Cast effect","x":-2178,"y":2622,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"621ec32c636b2fe0","type":"text","text":"Start by adding an OnSelfCast trigger. Cast triggers are activated from the card itself, and as such, don't need to be connected to signals. You can add ConditionalComponents to it to make it so the cast fails if conditions aren't met.","x":-2241,"y":2782,"width":376,"height":180},
		{"id":"c74230ad44021467","type":"text","text":"WIP: When a cast fails, a printout needs to be made to the battle log explaining the reason.","x":-1683,"y":2813,"width":250,"height":119},
		{"id":"429b22776738ac35","type":"text","text":"Add a CardAction as a child to your OnSelfCastTrigger with the Add Child Node (+) button. ","x":-2252,"y":3042,"width":398,"height":100},
		{"id":"8eff02436c3cbcb9","type":"text","text":"Add a ManualTargetingComponent or an AutoTargetingComponent.","x":-2209,"y":3202,"width":313,"height":120},
		{"id":"99d1d44784d70f77","type":"text","text":"Add any number of Skill children to your CardAction. All of them would be applied to each card in the list returned by your TargetingComponent.","x":-2243,"y":3402,"width":380,"height":140},
		{"id":"e4bc9f2a023f9fa0","type":"text","text":"ManualTargetingComponents can also accept ConditionalComponent children. When you use one, make sure to set its ManualTargetingGroup! It's set to NONE by default.","x":-1745,"y":3189,"width":375,"height":147},
		{"id":"f45ef54851f336cd","type":"text","text":"WIP: Add an animation which shows which cards the player can target","x":-1246,"y":3203,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"c90d5e896f93076f","type":"text","text":"Does the TargetingComponent under the CardAction child of Trigger return at least one eligible target? ","x":1400,"y":131,"width":280,"height":119},
		{"id":"79bb0419e933a50e","type":"text","text":"The CardAction fails. All subsequent CardActions under the same Trigger also fail. The Trigger's execute() function returns False.","x":1415,"y":-140,"width":250,"height":165},
		{"id":"a7ef5050b94c8445","type":"text","text":"Are there Skill children of the CardAction which hadn't yet executed their effects?","x":1820,"y":138,"width":250,"height":105},
		{"id":"16c00e1c9cdee99d","type":"text","text":"Proceed to the next Skill child. This happens regardless of whether or not the Skill succeeded or failed.","x":1820,"y":-100,"width":250,"height":150},
		{"id":"8fd4045ecfe56f91","type":"text","text":"Are there any more CardActions under the same Trigger?","x":2180,"y":145,"width":250,"height":90},
		{"id":"9ce224c082c537f4","type":"text","text":"If there are several CardAction nodes under one Trigger, they are activated in order. If one of them fails, all others fail as well. This could be used to make it so that if, say, the player chooses not to sacrifice an ally or cannot do so, the action cannot proceed.","x":-762,"y":1492,"width":332,"height":208},
		{"id":"e8dbdbb94a2ba583","type":"text","text":"Put two CardAction nodes under a Trigger.","x":-721,"y":1762,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5a4d6cc5da38cc08","type":"text","text":"So you want to...","x":-721,"y":1182,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3009ca64832da3ca","type":"text","text":"Create a sacrifice action: the player needs to choose one of their cards to sacrifice to gain a benefit.","x":-721,"y":1302,"width":250,"height":140},
		{"id":"8221ef1be31a0bd1","type":"text","text":"The first CardAction represents the cost. ","x":-721,"y":1872,"width":250,"height":85},
		{"id":"495e95e88a61da96","type":"text","text":"So you want to...","x":-82,"y":1179,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e906235535f3ddfd","type":"text","text":"Parent SkillSendToGraveyard to the CardAction so that the chosen card is destroyed.","x":-741,"y":1989,"width":291,"height":126},
		{"id":"0e68b1bcad675b43","type":"text","text":"The second CardAction represents the payoff. If the first one activated successfully, this one activates to deliver the reward.","x":-741,"y":2161,"width":291,"height":163},
		{"id":"1544f7fa870f8318","type":"text","text":"Can multiple CardAction nodes under the same Trigger all have a ManualTargetingComponent? Absolutely! The game will wait until the player makes or aborts the choice.","x":-760,"y":2380,"width":330,"height":157},
		{"id":"b4b7995785c21c7b","type":"text","text":"Create a skill whose numbers scale dynamically?","x":-88,"y":1302,"width":262,"height":60},
		{"id":"58200f4db4e3b5e2","type":"text","text":"This can be done by parenting ScalingComponent children to the Skill. If the Skill has integer export vars whose value is more than 0, it will be replaced by the value returned by the ScalingComponent.","x":-109,"y":1426,"width":305,"height":194},
		{"id":"38c83ebcd615e1be","type":"text","text":"TargetingComponents run all cards within a chosen group through their ConditionalComponent children to determine which ones can be targeted They determine 'group y' a card's effect text that goes 'on z: do x to the group y'","x":1400,"y":372,"width":280,"height":228},
		{"id":"9850ce1d8ad0a21d","type":"text","text":"WIP: Make sure that every single value in existing skills conforms to this rule.","x":320,"y":1476,"width":250,"height":94},
		{"id":"7a5ec73bd33df8af","type":"text","text":"Press New Inherited Scene and inherit from Cards/card.tscn","x":-420,"y":-321,"width":250,"height":100},
		{"id":"3a6f4e3dd76d7e25","type":"text","text":"Set up variables in main node","x":-420,"y":-161,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a9988f1ff42c450a","type":"text","text":"Set the art","x":-420,"y":-61,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5ea0ef6dd550279f","type":"text","text":"Add Keywords","x":-420,"y":45,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"decc4e0749180d5c","type":"text","text":"Skills represent individual effects applied to every target card. They determine the x in 'on z: do x to group y'","x":1820,"y":441,"width":250,"height":159},
		{"id":"1767eefd43c92432","x":2580,"y":128,"width":292,"height":115,"type":"text","text":"Execution is finished successfully, the Trigger's execute() function returns True"},
		{"id":"62a9527c4d449cad","x":1179,"y":1362,"width":124,"height":64,"type":"text","text":"Actions"},
		{"id":"43864ca0f87f4e00","x":1428,"y":1332,"width":250,"height":123,"type":"text","text":"Skills - direct effects that change cards' values and behaviors."},
		{"id":"e8dfa9cf9231d833","x":876,"y":1242,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"CardScriptsAndComponents"},
		{"id":"a89661a657bce90f","x":1150,"y":1242,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"< GO THERE FOR CARD LOGIC PARTS"},
		{"id":"5db998ddf94df852","x":1428,"y":1491,"width":250,"height":149,"type":"text","text":"ConditionalComponents - compare two cards together in a certain way and return true or false. Used to set up conditions for cards' effects."},
		{"id":"b1fcc92793872ffa","x":1179,"y":1534,"width":144,"height":64,"type":"text","text":"Conditionals"},
		{"id":"692e06dc06c479d7","x":1179,"y":1714,"width":181,"height":78,"type":"text","text":"EffectCounters"},
		{"id":"876a8a076f5a266d","x":1430,"y":1710,"width":250,"height":86,"type":"text","text":"Temporary status effects that can stack and function like their own Actions nodes."},
		{"id":"bcf332eec91584a2","x":1181,"y":1874,"width":179,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"Keywords"},
		{"id":"a53f0df67602b0db","x":1430,"y":1846,"width":250,"height":106,"type":"text","text":"Permanent card properties which fundamentally change how a card behaves."},
		{"id":"ec63c712137e4514","x":1178,"y":2004,"width":222,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"ScalingComponents"},
		{"id":"3734dcfdbab876de","x":1760,"y":1869,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Parent them to Card's MyKeywords node!"},
		{"id":"2fc334f9a1f76cc9","x":1760,"y":1536,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Can be parented to Triggers and TargetingComponents."},
		{"id":"fd4ad9b90cc082e8","x":1760,"y":1362,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Parent them to CardActions"},
		{"id":"5545a1ca1d62df0e","x":1430,"y":1995,"width":250,"height":68,"type":"text","text":"Parent them to Skills to adjust the numbers they use."},
		{"id":"073c16bc208c67fc","x":1171,"y":2140,"width":229,"height":50,"type":"text","text":"TargetingComponents"},
		{"id":"23e34457ace0bfde","x":1430,"y":2126,"width":250,"height":78,"type":"text","text":"Return a set of Cards for Skills to affect."},
		{"id":"6db8063d823ba790","x":1760,"y":2135,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Parent them to CardActions"},
		{"id":"aafb73b2bb438f02","x":1171,"y":2256,"width":189,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Triggers"},
		{"id":"16fd07c94b439f65","x":1430,"y":2256,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Activate CardActions when a certain signal is emitted."},
		{"id":"20c88ad443890558","x":1760,"y":2256,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Parent them to Card's Actions node!"},
		{"id":"ff33781f5d8fdfab","x":2070,"y":1239,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Art"},
		{"id":"208b1d97c1236b32","x":2320,"y":1334,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Card Art"},
		{"id":"1c2fcdcdadee0014","x":2640,"y":1334,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Put art for Cards there!"},
		{"id":"b3f9818f01a5e460","x":2320,"y":1461,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"CardComponents"},
		{"id":"c130583ae6ecfdb6","x":2640,"y":1461,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Put art for Effect Counters there!"},
		{"id":"9b4520151ed2eead","x":2323,"y":1588,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Portraits"},
		{"id":"40deb4e6a0ef9c2c","x":2640,"y":1588,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Put Champion portraits there!"},
		{"id":"490007f2afa1f3b8","x":1583,"y":961,"width":427,"height":218,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"<span style=\"font-size:40px\">CARD COMPONENT DIRECTORY MEMORANDUM!</span>"},
		{"id":"0cf0038adf0779e1","type":"text","text":"<span style=\"font-size:40px\">So you want to create a card\n","x":-485,"y":-580,"width":380,"height":186,"color":"2"}
	],
